From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] context: the control-plane client

resolve and keys ask the control plane's dashboard socket, a Unix socket, presenting the
assertion. A call is bounded in time and its answer in size; an answer is checked member by
member before use, the connection strings against the one accepted form, and only checked
members are kept. A resolve answer lives in memory per (ref, iss, sub, role class), its 60 s
counted as elapsed time, and, encrypted with AES-256-GCM under the node's cache key and bound
to the project and role class, on disk. The disk entry is read only when the socket gives no
answer, and not once the socket's last answer is older than the entry's lifetime, by the
file's time and by the time inside the answer; a refusal is final. Temporary files an
interrupted write left are removed before the next write. The module's settings are read at
the first use, or by checkSettings; a missing or malformed one stops the process.
